From aa50378e8490bf648c562dc20b929ac616e7dc5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gaston Rodriguez <gastonr@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:07:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/32] Strip unrendered head tags from sanitized clipboard
 markup

CreateStrictlyProcessedMarkupWithContext can preserve <base>, <link>,
and <meta> in its fast serialization path because the parser's scripting
and plugin restrictions do not remove them. If an application inserts
the sanitized output into a document, these elements can change URL
resolution, load resources, or trigger navigation.

This CL explicitly removes these three HTML element types from the
parsed fragment on each sanitization iteration before choosing a
serialization path or attaching the fragment to the staging document.

Added parameterized coverage for each tag: adjacent and nested removal
with exact preservation of other markup, inline display overrides, and
stylesheet display overrides with legitimate style conversion preserved.

